%N A399853 Number of strongly connected digraphs on n labeled nodes, reducible as a flow graph rooted at node 1 and also rooted at node 2, in which every proper region block of the decomposition rooted at node 1 avoiding node 2 is a single node.
%C A399853 These self-cores are the kernels obtained by collapsing each region block that avoids node 2 to its entry. The roots are the fixed nodes 1 and 2, not an elected pair.
%C A399853 The region decomposition rooted at node 1 is recursive: delete the entry, take the strongly connected components, and recurse within each non-singleton component from its unique entry. The whole graph is not a proper block. All digraphs here have no self-loops.
%C A399853 In the formula, E ranges over subsets of {(i,j): 1<=i,j<=n, i!=j}, D_E is the corresponding digraph, B_1(D_E) is its set of proper region blocks rooted at node 1, and [P] is 1 when P holds and 0 otherwise. The summation is restricted to strongly connected D_E reducible from both nodes 1 and 2.
%D A399853 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A399853 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A399853 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A399853 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A399853 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A399853 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A399853 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Python program (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%F A399853 a(n) = Sum_{E: D_E strong and reducible from 1 and 2} Product_{B in B_1(D_E); 2 not in B} [|B|=1].
